From 3ad5a23b829efd86870855afdd240180979e1145 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: StachowiakDawid <dawidos234@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:38:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] phy: exynos5-usbdrd: add Exynos9820 host mode, USB3 and
 DisplayPort combo PHY

Exynos 9820 support for the USB DRD PHY, with its binding:

 - USB 2.0 host mode (software controlled VBUS valid, over-current
   from the unused SET_OCD bits).
 - The USB3 half of the USBDP combo PHY, enabled with exynos9820_ss=1
   (default off: USB 2.0 only): PMA init in the vendor EVT1 sequence
   with the PCS PLL enable forced (the LC PLL does not start
   otherwise), the vendor SuperSpeed tune set applied before the PLL
   starts and again on the running PMA, and a reported RX CDR lock
   wait. A lock failure falls back to USB 2.0 instead of failing
   phy_init().
 - The SuperSpeed lanes follow the Type-C orientation switch when a
   cable is attached, else the port select GPIO; they are re-targeted
   on phy_set_mode() when the orientation changed.
 - An HS pull-up hold (PHY_MODE_USB_DEVICE_SS/_HS) for
   SuperSpeed-first connects.
 - DisplayPort mode of the combo PHY as a third PHY, with the EVT1
   default table; powering DP on stops USB3.
 - The probe is deferred until the port select GPIO is available.
 - The host column of the SuperSpeed tune uses RX EQ 0xc / DFE tap 0
   like the other Exynos 9820 boards; with the Galaxy S10+ vendor
   values the link behind a USB3 hub on lanes 0/1 dropped under
   traffic.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: StachowiakDawid <dawidos234@gmail.com>
